Open your terminal window.

First, navigate to the example directory by typing:
cd examples/02_md_sample

To avoid typing your API key and model name every time, you can set them in a configuration file in standard locations.
 dragiter automatically looks for a default user config file at ~/.config/dragiter/config.toml.

 Alternatively, you can use the -c flag to point to a specific TOML config file, or use environment variables like DRAGITER_API_KEY.

 It is highly recommended to run a simulation first.
 This allows you to verify the workflow without making actual API calls or spending credits.
 You can do this by adding the -s flag to your command.

Run the simulation by typing:
dragiter -s -p 02_prompt_c_sample.toml -r 02_resource_c_sample.toml

Once you confirm the simulation output looks correct, run the actual process by removing the -s flag:
dragiter -p 02_prompt_c_sample.toml -r 02_resource_c_sample.toml
